	"name": "Pine Shrine Wall (harder)",
	"_design": "Stage 2 (monster levels 2-3, a step up from the Ink Garden). A pine-ridge shrine: the player starts in the south yard (painted ink ground), a broken shrine wall with five 3-unit gates (plus open ends at both sides) runs across the whole stage, and north of it lies a pale paved shrine yard with a reflecting pool under an ancient plum. Every monster starts north of the player and heads for them at once (no aggro radius yet), so the gates are choke points: hold a gate and they come through one or two at a time, or get flanked from two gates. The wall is only 1.5 high so monsters behind it stay readable from camera 8, and its segments are at most 8 long so the detouring AI always finds a gate. The second rest point is inside the shrine yard: healing means pushing through the wall. Entering the yard pulls the camera back a little (camera zone) so the final fight with two brutes reads as a whole. Tall trees stand only outside the walkable bounds, never south of a fight. Monsters (2026-10-12): four level-2 goblins come first; the shrine yard holds a level-3 goblin mage (east), a level-3 goblin knight (west, the yard fight) and a goblin archer in the far north-east corner (the wall blocks arrows, so it only shoots through gates or once the player is in the yard).",
